"Prevent corefiles from being overwritten, if ``kernel.core_pattern`` is "
"something simple like ``\"core\"``."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.rename_corefiles:7
msgid ""
"Ensure corefiles are generated, if ``kernel.core_pattern`` uses "
"``apport``, which refuses to overwrite any existing files."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.rename_corefiles:10
msgid "This only affects corefiles accessed via :attr:`.process.corefile`."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.rename_corefiles:12
msgid "Default value is ``True``."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.sign:1 pwnlib.context.ContextType.signedness:1
msgid "Alias for :attr:`signed`"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.signed:1
msgid "Signed-ness for packing operation when it's not explicitly set."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.signed:3
msgid ""
"Can be set to any non-string truthy value, or the specific string values "
"``'signed'`` or ``'unsigned'`` which are converted into :const:`True` and"
" :const:`False` correspondingly."
msgstr ""

#: ../pwntools/docs/docstring of pwnlib.context.ContextType.signednesses:1
msgid "Valid string values for :attr:`signed`"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.silent:1
msgid "Disable all non-error logging within the enclosed scope."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.terminal:1
msgid ""
"Default terminal used by :meth:`pwnlib.util.misc.run_in_new_terminal`. "
"Can be a string or an iterable of strings.  In the latter case the first "
"entry is the terminal and the rest are default arguments."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.terminal:7
msgid ""
":meth:`pwnlib.util.misc.run_in_new_terminal` has special handlers for "
"supported terminals with windowing capabilities, which might apply to "
"terminals set with this context option. See its documentation for "
"additional information on this behavior."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.throw_eof_on_incomplete_line:1
msgid ""
"Whether to raise an :class:`EOFError` if an EOF is received before a "
"newline in ``tube.recvline``."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.throw_eof_on_incomplete_line:3
msgid ""
"Controls if an :class:`EOFError` is treated as newline in "
"``tube.recvline`` and similar functions and whether a warning should be "
"logged about it."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.throw_eof_on_incomplete_line:8
msgid ""
"``True``: Raise an :class:`EOFError` if an EOF is received before a "
"newline."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.throw_eof_on_incomplete_line:9
msgid ""
"``False``: Return the data received so far if an EOF is received before a"
" newline without logging a warning."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.throw_eof_on_incomplete_line:11
msgid ""
"``None``: Return the data received so far if an EOF is received before a "
"newline and log a warning."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.throw_eof_on_incomplete_line:14
msgid "Default value is ``None``."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.timeout:1
msgid ""
"Default amount of time to wait for a blocking operation before it times "
"out, specified in seconds."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.timeout:4
msgid "The default value is to have an infinite timeout."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.timeout:6
msgid ""
"See :class:`pwnlib.timeout.Timeout` for additional information on valid "
"values."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.verbose:1
msgid "Enable all logging within the enclosed scope."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.verbose:3
msgid "This is the opposite of :attr:`.quiet` and functionally equivalent to:"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.verbose:12
msgid "Note that the function does not emit any information by default"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.verbose:18
msgid ""
"But if we put it inside a :attr:`.verbose` context manager, the "
"information is printed."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.windbg_binary:1
msgid "Path to the binary that is used when running WinDbg locally."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.windbg_binary:3
msgid ""
"This is useful when you have multiple versions of WinDbg installed or the"
" WinDbg binary is called something different."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.windbg_binary:6
msgid ""
"Usually, it is installed to ``C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Windows "
"Kits\\10\\Debuggers\\x64\\windbg.exe``. Adding the path to the Windows "
"SDK to your PATH variable is recommended."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.windbg_binary:9
msgid ""
"If set to an empty string, pwntools will try to search for a reasonable "
"WinDbg binary from the path."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.windbgx_binary:1
msgid "Path to the binary that is used when running WinDbgX locally."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.windbgx_binary:3
msgid ""
"This is useful when you have multiple versions of WinDbgX installed or "
"the WinDbgX binary is called something different."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.windbgx_binary:6
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Usually, it is installed to "
"``%LocalAppData%\\Microsoft\\WindowsApps\\WinDbgX.exe``."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.windbgx_binary:8
msgid ""
"If set to an empty string, pwntools will try to search for a reasonable "
"WinDbgX binary from the path."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.word_size:1
msgid "Alias for :attr:`bits`"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.x64dbg_binary:1
msgid "Path to the binary that is used when running x64dbg locally."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.x64dbg_binary:3
msgid ""
"Should be set to the x96dbg.exe launcher binary to handle 32-bit and "
"64-bit binaries."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.x64dbg_binary:5
msgid ""
"This is useful when you have multiple versions of x64dbg installed or the"
" x64dbg binary is called something different."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.context.ContextType.x64dbg_binary:8
msgid ""
"If set to an empty string, pwntools will try to search for a reasonable "
"x64dbg binary from the path or based on the ``\"Debug with x64dbg\"`` "
"shell extension if available."
msgstr ""

#: ../pwntools/docs/docstring of pwnlib.context.context:1
msgid ""
"Global :class:`.ContextType` object, used to store commonly-used pwntools"
" settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../pwntools/docs/docstring of pwnlib.context.context:3
msgid ""
"In most cases, the context is used to infer default variables values. For"
" example, :func:`.asm` can take an ``arch`` parameter as a keyword "
"argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../pwntools/docs/docstring of pwnlib.context.context:7
msgid ""
"If it is not supplied, the ``arch`` specified by ``context`` is used "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../pwntools/docs/docstring of pwnlib.context.context:9
msgid ""
"Consider it a shorthand to passing ``os=`` and ``arch=`` to every single "
"function call."
msgstr ""

